  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive). Pattern: X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{足|た}りる (X is sufficient).\n\nASPECT: て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates ongoing state. {足|た}りて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ = 'is sufficient.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {足|た}りない (not enough—very common)\n- {足|た}りる (is enough)\n- ⟦これ→これ：00963_kore⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{足|た}りる (this is enough)\n- X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{足|た}りない (lacking X)\n- {足|た}りなく⟦なる→なる：01970_naru⟧ (run out of, become insufficient)\n\nNEGATIVE USAGE: This verb is very often used in the negative. {足|た}りない is one of the most common ways to express insufficiency.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{足|た}す→足す：01168_tasu⟧: to add (to make sufficient)\n- ⟦{十分|じゅうぶん}→十分：01614_juubun⟧: enough, sufficient (noun/na-adj)\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {足|た}りる: to be sufficient (ichidan verb)\n- ⟦{足|た}す→足す：01168_tasu⟧: to add (godan verb)\n\nThese are different verbs with related but distinct meanings.",
